== Effects ==
* Upon use, Isaac raises the candle above his head. On pressing a fire button, a blue flame, similar to a {{E|Blue Fire Place}}, will fire in the chosen direction, extinguishing itself after a fixed time of approximately two seconds.
* {{dlc|nr}} The flame deals 23 damage per damage tick.
** {{dlc|nr}} The maximum damage dealt by a single flame is around 276, dealing damage roughly 6 times per second.
* {{dlc|r}} The flame decreases in damage over time, starting at 23 per tick at max size, until it scales down to 11.5 per tick at minimum size.
** {{dlc|r}} The maximum damage dealt by a single flame is around 160, dealing damage roughly 6 times per second.
* The flame also destroys enemy shots it comes into contact with.

== Notes ==
* {{dlc|nr}} While Isaac holds the candle above his head, his movement speed is reduced.
* {{dlc|nr}} Will block Isaac's tears, unlike {{I|Red Candle}} and won't burn him.
* Flames do not drop any collectibles when doused.
* The flame can destroy {{e|Shopkeeper}}s.
* The flame projectile can pass over Pits, but can not travel through Rocks or Poop.
* The flames from this item can put out {{e|Fire Place}}s.
* {{dlc+|r}} The flame can ignite gas clouds such as ones found in {{s|Dross}}.{{dlc-}}

== Synergies ==
* {{Book of Virtues synergy|description=Spawns blue wisps on the middle ring. The wisps do not persist between rooms.}}

== Interactions ==
